## 1. Application Binary Interface (ABI)

The Application Binary Interface defines the conventions that allow compiled software components to work together.

It specifies:
- Function argument passing.
- Return-value conventions.
- Register usage.
- Stack organization.
- Calling conventions.

**ABI vs ISA**

- ISA defines the instructions supported by a processor.
- ABI defines how software components interact when using that instruction set.

