## 4. Load, Add and Store Instructions

RISC-V follows a load-store architecture.

- Load: transfers data from memory into a register.
- Add: performs arithmetic using register values.
- Store: transfers data from a register into memory.

Example RV64I instructions:

```asm
ld  x8, 16(x23)
add x8, x24, x8
sd  x8, 8(x23)
```

